From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: gdk: import LINEAR dmabufs into EGL without an explicit modifier

freedreno on the Adreno 306 advertises no explicit modifiers for R8 / GR88,
the per-plane formats GTK uses to sample NV12, so importing a camera NV12
dmabuf tagged DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR fails ("Creating EGLImage for dmabuf
failed") and GTK falls back to an mmap download + upload every frame, while
the same planes import fine with the implicit modifier (which is linear on
msm). Leave the modifier out for LINEAR buffers.
---
--- a/gdk/gdkdmabufegl.c
+++ b/gdk/gdkdmabufegl.c
@@ -310,7 +310,8 @@

 #define ADD_PLANE(plane) \
   { \
-    if (dmabuf->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID) \
+    if (dmabuf->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID && \
+        dmabuf->modifier != DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR) \
       { \
         attribs[i++] = EGL_DMA_BUF_PLANE## plane ##_MODIFIER_LO_EXT; \
         attribs[i++] = dmabuf->modifier & 0xFFFFFFFF; \
